272
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:31,930
Right.

273
00:13:32,730 --> 00:13:34,140
Because girls are always like,

274
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:36,250
"Ooh, that guy owns two Star Trek uniforms

275
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:37,610
"and gets a lot of ear infections.

276
00:13:37,610 --> 00:13:39,780
I got to get me some of that."

277
00:13:42,130 --> 00:13:42,630
I don't know,

278
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:44,380
I bet it happens more than you realize.

279
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:45,880
Trust me, it doesn't.

280
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,270
You sure?

281
00:13:47,270 --> 00:13:49,270
You're cute, you're funny.

282
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:51,990
Maybe you're getting hit on, and you don't even know it.

283
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,460
Really?

284
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,090
I'm pretty sure

285
00:14:05,110 --> 00:14:06,070
Okay, I got to get back to work.

286
00:14:06,070 --> 00:14:07,560
Thanks for listening.

287
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:09,670
No problem.

288
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:12,820
Hope-hope no girls rip my clothes off on the way.

289
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:19,090
Come on, we're smart guys.

290
00:14:19,090 --> 00:14:21,650
- We can figure this out. - Forty-three.

291
00:14:21,650 --> 00:14:24,160
What is 43?

292
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:27,420
Besides my mom's neck size.

293
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:32,210
It's the atomic number for technetium.

294
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:34,480
That stuff's radioactive.

295
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:36,880
Do you think he's building a bomb?

296
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,750
It took him two years to put together

297
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:40,600
that Lego Death Star; I'm not worried.

298
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:45,030
Ooh, this could be something.

299
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:47,290
43 is the number of calories

300
00:14:47,290 --> 00:14:50,150
in half a cup of fat-free yogurt.

301
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,630
Why would you know that?

302
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:54,350
I'm sorry.

303
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:57,340
We can't all eat whatever we want and still stay thin.

304
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,340
Wait, in the Hitchhikers Guide to the Galaxy,

305
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,180
isn't 43 the answer to the question

306
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:08,280
of life, the universe, and everything?

307
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:11,280
That's 42, dumb-ass.

308
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:15,050
Feelings.

309
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,860
We should stop.

310
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:19,820
- I'm exhausted. - Yeah, me, too.

311
00:15:19,830 --> 00:15:21,430
We've got more important things to do.

312
00:15:21,430 --> 00:15:23,190
Who cares what stupid 43 means?

313
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,450
- Not me. - Let's go home.

314
00:15:27,730 --> 00:15:28,900
You want to get something to eat?

315
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,590
Sounds good.

316
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,400
What the balls is 43?!

317
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,680
I have to know!

318
00:15:42,950 --> 00:15:45,380
Hey, shouldn't you be out with your gang,

319
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:48,460
spray painting equations on the side of buildings?

320
00:15:49,930 --> 00:15:51,380
Come on, I'm sorry.

321
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:52,960
I just can't believe you don't trust me.

322
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:54,570
I do, of course I do.

323
00:15:54,570 --> 00:15:56,500
Then why did you embarrass me in front of my friend,

324
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:59,060
who, by the way, knew exactly who you were?

325
00:15:59,060 --> 00:16:02,060
- Really? - Your picture's on my refrigerator.

326
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,660
You know, I'm really starting to not like this guy.

327
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:10,990
What is your problem?

328
00:16:10,990 --> 00:16:12,530
Do you use up all your thinking at work

329
00:16:12,530 --> 00:16:14,800
and then have none left over for when you get home?

330
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,000
I don't know.

331
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,690
It's hard sometimes.

332
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:20,060
Everywhere you go,

333
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:23,050
guys hit on you, even if I'm standing right there.

334
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:24,390
And they're all taller than me.

335
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:26,730
Why is everyone taller than me?

336
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:30,280
You know what, this is all in my head.

337
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,970
It's my problem, not yours.

338
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:33,650
Leonard, why do you always do this?

339
00:16:33,650 --> 00:16:35,520
Listen to me, you're the one I'm with.

340
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,750
You know I love you, so will you please relax

341
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:39,780
because you're driving me crazy.

342
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:49,470
You know that's the first time you ever said that you love me.

343
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:52,450
Yeah.

344
00:16:56,670 --> 00:16:59,890
We're just supposed to pretend it's not a big deal?

345
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:03,520
That's...

346
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:08,230
exactly what we're gonna do because...

347
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:10,190
you're about to make me cry,

348
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:13,000
and we both know if I start crying,

349
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,510
you're gonna start crying.

350
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,550
- You're right, you should go. - All right.

351
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:30,120
She loves me.

352
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:36,020
"Hey, it's Alex.

353
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:37,200
Nice having coffee with you.

354
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,980
If you want to talk more, I'm always available.

355
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,380
Smiley face, smiley face."

356
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:43,620
What a friendly girl.

357
00:17:48,510 --> 00:17:50,240
Okay, picture's up.

358
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,040
Looks like the camera's working.

359
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,580
That's good quality video.

360
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:56,950
It better be. It's the spare camera for the Mars rover.

361
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:59,250
How did you get your hands on that?

362
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:00,950
Million dollar camera--

363
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:02,750
ten dollar lock.

364
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,960
Oh, my God, here he comes.

365
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,690
This is it.

366
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,900
What the hell is that thing?

367
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:19,170
I don't know.

368
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:20,710
This is Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

369
00:18:20,710 --> 00:18:22,670
Experimental log.

370
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:27,410
Wormhole generator test 44.

371
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:30,250
Wormhole generator test?

372
00:18:34,910 --> 00:18:37,370
The first 43 parallel universes

373
00:18:37,370 --> 00:18:40,160
I've checked proved to be empty.

374
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,710
I see no reason to suspect

375
00:18:41,710 --> 00:18:44,730
universe number 44 will be any different.

376
00:18:51,070 --> 00:18:52,770
Oh, my God!

377
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:54,680
Holy crap!

378
00:19:01,130 --> 00:19:03,540
It's eating my face!

379
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,290
It's eating his face!

380
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:14,550
I found your Webcam and replaced the video feed.

381
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:16,840
You two should be ashamed of yourselves.

382
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,460
Sheldon, we're really sorry.

383
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,570
Yeah, really sorry.

384
00:19:19,570 --> 00:19:20,940
Sorry?

385
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,370
You may not realize it,

386
00:19:22,370 --> 00:19:25,900
but I have difficulty navigating certain aspects of daily life.

387
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,640
You know, understanding sarcasm,

388
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,210
feigning interest in others,

389
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:34,050
not talking about trains as much as I want to.

390
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,320
It's exhausting.

391
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:38,280
Which is why, for 20 minutes a day,

392
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,080
I like to go down to that room,

393
00:19:40,090 --> 00:19:41,420
turn my mind off

394
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:43,790
and do what I need to do to recharge.

395
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:46,890
But what are you doing in there?

396
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:48,490
And what does 43 mean?

397
00:19:48,490 --> 00:19:49,930
You don't need to know,

398
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:51,460
you don't deserve to know,

399
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,460
and you will never know.

400
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:58,400
Yeah, well I know how to make your egg salad now.

401
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:44,260
One, two, three, four,

402
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:48,400
five, six, seven, eight...

403
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,290
Drat.

404
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:55,700
I'm never going to get to 43 again.

405
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:59,720
One, two, three, four...

406
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:01,640
Rats.

